      "message": "Yet you\u0027re saying that we can still depend on the unstable parts of the headers (which may be more behavioral, and not caught by linking against stubs). Why would we want to build them differently? Especially since it means that these two (valid) ways of saying the same thing will give different build results:\n\n cc_library {\n   name: \"libfoo\",\n   srcs: [\"*.c\"],\n   shared_libs: [\"libY\"],\n }\n\nvs\n\n cc_library_shared {\n   name: \"libfoo\",\n   whole_static_libs: [\"libfoo_static\"],\n   shared_libs: [\"libY\"],\n }\n\n cc_library_static {\n   name: \"libfoo_static\",\n   srcs: [\"*.c\"],\n   shared_libs: [\"libY\"],\n }\n\nThis was a very common way to declare libraries in Make, though we don\u0027t see it as often with cc_library in soong.",
